The '''N5 sentry droid''',<ref name="Handbook" /> also known as the '''New Republic Security Droid''', was a model of [[security droid]]<ref name="SWCT">{{SWCT|set=2021 Base|cardname=New Republic Security Droid}}</ref> that existed in the [[Imperial Era]]<ref name="Book of Ajax">{{StoryCite|story=The Book of Ajax|book=Dark Droids: D-Squad 1}}</ref> and later [[New Republic Era]], where it would be used by the [[New Republic Correctional Corps]].<ref name="Chapter 6" />

==Description==
the N5 sentry Droid had a [[humanoid]] appearance with gray plating along with a singular yellow optic in its head module with a boxy main body.

It's outer material appears to be made of a relatively weak metal as a [[vibroblade]] is easily able to cut and penetrate it

==History==
One N5 who managed to think for themself joined the ranks of the [[Second Revelation]] and was present for the [[droid]] revolutionary [[Ajax Sigma]]'s return, where the former [[Soldier|warrior]] decreed that they should stay at the [[Colony of the Second Revelation|colony]] as a new home.<ref name="Book of Ajax" /> There, Ajax formed the group into a droid church.<ref name="Dark Droids 1">[[Dark Droids 1|''Dark Droids'' 1]]</ref>

[[File:N5SentryDroids-TMCh6.png|thumb|300px|left|N5 security droids were stationed on board prison transport ''Bothan-5''.]]
N5 [[droid]]s were used aboard [[New Republic Correctional Transport]]s. When boarding a [[prison]] [[transport]], the ''[[Bothan-5]]'', to [[Bothan-Five incident|rescue]] the [[prisoner]] [[Qin]], a team of [[Mercenary|mercenaries]] recruited by [[Ranzar Malk]] encountered a number of the security droids. The droids were destroyed by the [[bounty hunter]] known as [[Din Djarin|the Mandalorian]]. The team later betrayed the Mandalorian, trapping him in a cell, but the bounty hunter pulled a security droid towards him with a [[grappling hook]] and tore off its [[Limb|arm]], destroyed its head, which was a weak spot, and used the arm to unlock the door.<ref name="Chapter 6" /> Mayfield also shot three droids while fleeing. These droids were also used in the [[Karthon Chop Fields]]. [[Unidentified N5 sentry droid|One]] of them gave new instructions to [[Migs Mayfeld]] to follow [[Carasynthia Dune]].<ref name="Chapter 15" />

